\date{2025-10-25T04:05:52Z}
\title{Pronunciation and origin of “Yorgey”}

\p{My last name is pronounced “YOR-ghee” (/'jɔːrgi/), with a hard G sound, a long E at the end, and with the stress falling on the first syllable. It is not pronounced “yor-gay” or “yor-jee” (the two most common mispronunciations I hear). It is probably derived from the Greek word γεωργός (“farmer”, literally γη + ἔργον = “earth-worker”) although no one knows for sure. If you are ever in Lancaster County in southeastern Pennsylvania, you can take your clothes to [Yorgey's Fine Dry Cleaning](https://www.yorgeys.com/locations.php), which was founded by my great-grandfather.}

\p{My username has always been \code{byorgey} pretty much everywhere online (gmail, IRC, Discord, [Mastodon](https://mathstodon.xyz/@byorgey), [Hanab Live](https://hanab.live)...), ever since it was my automatically assigned [Williams Students Online](https://wso.williams.edu/#) UNIX username in the fall of 2000.  If you need to pronounce it out loud (\em{e.g.} if you are doing a voice chat review of a Hanabi game with me), you can pronounce it just like my last name but with an extra "b" sound at the beginning.  Alternatively, you can just say "Brent".}
